QueryPage.tsx:170 flattens the two fields into one string — `const message = [subject, "", body].join("
")` — and posts it as the `questions` payload (:171). The server never treats it as an email: buildQueryEmail (outbox.ts:229-239) mints its OWN subject, `Action needed: a few questions about ${deckName}`, and wraps the payload in its own greeting and sign-off — `${greeting}

Thanks for submitting ${deckName} to the programme. Before we can complete the review, our team needs a little more detail:

${questions}

...`. The founder therefore gets: a subject the operator never wrote and never saw; the operator's subject line buried as plain text in the middle of the body; and two stacked greetings ('Hi Ananya,' from the server, then 'Dear Founder,' from the composed body at shared/queries.ts:54). The file's own header comment at QueryPage.tsx:13-14 claims 'what is on screen is what the founder receives', which is false. The Subject input on this screen is decorative.
